's beds had a hospitalized patient during the period divided by (y) total number of beds, times (ii) total number of days during the period."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["5) Intravenous chemotherapy and radiotherapy infusions in both inpatient and outpatient care; excludes oral treatments. In Peru, includes sessions across the Healthcare Services Network and OncoSalud Segments."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["6) As of period end and as reported to the National Superintendence of Health Susalud in Peru."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["7) Insured population assigned to Auna under risk-sharing agreements in Colombia."]},"\n\n"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["About Auna"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["Auna is one of Latin America’s leading healthcare platforms, with operations in Mexico, Peru, and Colombia. It prioritizes prevention and focuses on complex diseases that represent the highest healthcare spending. Its mission is to transform healthcare by delivering access to a highly integrated offering of services in low-penetration markets across Spanish-speaking Latin America. Founded in 1989, Auna has built one of the region’s largest modern healthcare platforms, consisting of a horizontally integrated network of medical care centers and a vertically integrated portfolio of oncology and general health plans. As of September 30, 2026, Auna’s network included 31 healthcare facilities—hospitals, ambulatory centers, and prevention and wellness centers—with a total of 2,361 beds and 1.4 million health plan members."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Preliminary Information"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["The information contained in this press release is preliminary in nature and is provided for informational purposes only. It is based on current estimates, assumptions, and expectations, which remain subject to ongoing review, verification, and possibl